{"id":"mahabharata-5-181","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":181,"title":"एकाशीत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 181 · The battle continues","summary":{"en":"The fight goes on for days with divine weapons on both sides; Bhishma's charioteer tends the horses and Bhishma himself is tended by his mother Ganga. Each day ends with neither victorious.","kn":"ಎರಡೂ ಕಡೆ ದಿವ್ಯಾಸ್ತ್ರಗಳೊಂದಿಗೆ ಯುದ್ಧ ದಿನಗಟ್ಟಲೆ ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುತ್ತದೆ; ಭೀಷ್ಮನ ಸಾರಥಿ ಕುದುರೆಗಳನ್ನು ಉಪಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಪ್ರತಿ ದಿನವೂ ಯಾರೂ ಗೆಲ್ಲದೆ ಮುಗಿಯುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"दोनों ओर से दिव्यास्त्रों के साथ युद्ध कई दिन चलता है; भीष्म का सारथि घोड़ों की देखभाल करता है। हर दिन बिना किसी की विजय के समाप्त होता है।","te":"రెండు వైపులా దివ్యాస్త్రాలతో యుద్ధం రోజుల తరబడి సాగుతుంది; భీష్ముని సారథి గుర్రాలకు ఉపచారం చేస్తాడు. ప్రతి రోజూ ఎవరూ గెలవకుండానే ముగుస్తుంది.","ta":"இரு பக்கமும் தெய்வீக அஸ்திரங்களுடன் போர் பல நாட்கள் தொடர்கிறது; பீஷ்மரின் தேரோட்டி குதிரைகளைப் பராமரிக்கிறான். ஒவ்வொரு நாளும் யாரும் வெல்லாமல் முடிகிறது.","ml":"ദിവ്യാസ്ത്രങ്ങളുമായി ഇരുപക്ഷവും ദിവസങ്ങളോളം പൊരുതുന്നു; ഭീഷ്മരുടെ സാരഥി കുതിരകളെ പരിചരിക്കുന്നു; ഭീഷ്മരെ അമ്മ ഗംഗ ശുശ്രൂഷിക്കുന്നു. ഓരോ ദിവസവും ജയമാർക്കും ഇല്ലാതെ അവസാനിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.181; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"अम्बोपाख्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Ambopakhyana Parva (The story of Amba)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"आत्मनस्तु ततः सूतो हयानां च विशां पते ।\nमम चापनयामास शल्यान्कुशलसंमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then my charioteer, held skilled, drew the arrows out of himself, of the horses, and of me, lord of the people."}},{"n":2,"text":"स्नातोपवृत्तैस्तुरगैर्लब्धतोयैरविह्वलैः ।\nप्रभात उदिते सूर्ये ततो युद्धमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the horses bathed, exercised, watered and settled, the fight resumed at dawn when the sun rose."}},{"n":3,"text":"दृष्ट्वा मां तूर्णमायान्तं दंशितं स्यन्दने स्थितम् ।\nअकरोद्रथमत्यर्थं रामः सज्जं प्रतापवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing me coming swiftly, armored and standing in my chariot, mighty Rama made his chariot ready indeed."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततोऽहं राममायान्तं दृष्ट्वा समरकाङ्क्षिणम् ।\nधनुःश्रेष्ठं समुत्सृज्य सहसावतरं रथात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Rama coming, eager for battle, I put down my excellent bow and quickly got down from the chariot."}},{"n":5,"text":"अभिवाद्य तथैवाहं रथमारुह्य भारत ।\nयुयुत्सुर्जामदग्न्यस्य प्रमुखे वीतभीः स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After saluting him, I mounted the chariot again, Bharata, and stood fearless in front of Jamadagni's son, wanting to fight."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततो मां शरवर्षेण महता समवाकिरत् ।\nअहं च शरवर्षेण वर्षन्तं समवाकिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he covered me with a great shower of arrows, and I covered him as he showered, with a shower of arrows."}},{"n":7,"text":"संक्रुद्धो जामदग्न्यस्तु पुनरेव पतत्रिणः ।\nप्रेषयामास मे राजन्दीप्तास्यानुरगानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jamadagni's son, enraged, again sent winged arrows at me, king, like snakes with blazing mouths."}},{"n":8,"text":"तानहं निशितैर्भल्लैः शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ।\nअच्छिदं सहसा राजन्नन्तरिक्षे पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cut them down in the air, king, hundreds and thousands of them, again and again, with sharp broad-headed arrows."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततस्त्वस्त्राणि दिव्यानि जामदग्न्यः प्रतापवान् ।\nमयि प्रचोदयामास तान्यहं प्रत्यषेधयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then mighty Jamadagni's son sent divine weapons at me, and I countered them."}},{"n":10,"text":"अस्त्रैरेव महाबाहो चिकीर्षन्नधिकां क्रियाम् ।\nततो दिवि महान्नादः प्रादुरासीत्समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With weapons alone, mighty-armed one, wishing to do more, he did so; then a great roar arose in the sky on all sides."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततोऽहमस्त्रं वायव्यं जामदग्न्ये प्रयुक्तवान् ।\nप्रत्याजघ्ने च तद्रामो गुह्यकास्त्रेण भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I used the Vayavya weapon against Jamadagni's son, and Rama countered it with the Guhyaka weapon, Bharata."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततोऽस्त्रमहमाग्नेयमनुमन्त्र्य प्रयुक्तवान् ।\nवारुणेनैव रामस्तद्वारयामास मे विभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I fired the Agneya weapon, after invoking it, and Rama, the lord, stopped it with the Varuna weapon."}},{"n":13,"text":"एवमस्त्राणि दिव्यानि रामस्याहमवारयम् ।\nरामश्च मम तेजस्वी दिव्यास्त्रविदरिंदमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus I warded off Rama's divine weapons, and the radiant Rama, subduer of foes, who knew divine weapons, did the same to mine."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततो मां सव्यतो राजन्रामः कुर्वन्द्विजोत्तमः ।\nउरस्यविध्यत्संक्रुद्धो जामदग्न्यो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Rama, best of the twice-born, keeping me to his left, king, struck me in the chest, enraged, mighty Jamadagni's son."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततोऽहं भरतश्रेष्ठ संन्यषीदं रथोत्तमे ।\nअथ मां कश्मलाविष्टं सूतस्तूर्णमपावहत् ।\nगोरुतं भरतश्रेष्ठ रामबाणप्रपीडितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, best of Bharatas, I sank down in my fine chariot, and my charioteer quickly carried me off, dazed, tormented by Rama's arrows, to a cow-pen's distance."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततो मामपयातं वै भृशं विद्धमचेतसम् ।\nरामस्यानुचरा हृष्टाः सर्वे दृष्ट्वा प्रचुक्रुशुः ।\nअकृतव्रणप्रभृतयः काशिकन्या च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing me withdrawn, badly pierced and unconscious, all Rama's followers cried out with joy, Akritavrana and the rest, and the Kashi maiden, Bharata."}},{"n":17,"text":"ततस्तु लब्धसंज्ञोऽहं ज्ञात्वा सूतमथाब्रुवम् ।\nयाहि सूत यतो रामः सज्जोऽहं गतवेदनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having regained consciousness and understood, I said to my charioteer: Go where Rama is; I am ready, free of pain."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततो मामवहत्सूतो हयैः परमशोभितैः ।\nनृत्यद्भिरिव कौरव्य मारुतप्रतिमैर्गतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the charioteer carried me with his splendid horses, which seemed to dance, going like the wind, Kaurava."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततोऽहं राममासाद्य बाणजालेन कौरव ।\nअवाकिरं सुसंरब्धः संरब्धं विजिगीषया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Rama, Kaurava, I covered him, furious and wishing to win, with a net of arrows."}},{"n":20,"text":"तानापतत एवासौ रामो बाणानजिह्मगान् ।\nबाणैरेवाच्छिनत्तूर्णमेकैकं त्रिभिराहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama cut those straight-flying arrows as they came, three arrows against each one, quickly in that fight."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततस्ते मृदिताः सर्वे मम बाणाः सुसंशिताः ।\nरामबाणैर्द्विधा छिन्नाः शतशोऽथ महाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all my well-sharpened arrows were crushed, cut in two and in hundreds by Rama's arrows in the great battle."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततः पुनः शरं दीप्तं सुप्रभं कालसंमितम् ।\nअसृजं जामदग्न्याय रामायाहं जिघांसया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then again I hurled at Jamadagni's son Rama, wishing to kill him, a blazing, bright arrow like Time itself."}},{"n":23,"text":"तेन त्वभिहतो गाढं बाणच्छेदवशं गतः ।\nमुमोह सहसा रामो भूमौ च निपपात ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hit hard by it and fallen under the power of the arrow's cut, Rama suddenly fainted and fell to the ground."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततो हाहाकृतं सर्वं रामे भूतलमाश्रिते ।\nजगद्भारत संविग्नं यथार्कपतनेऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a cry of \"Alas!\" rose everywhere when Rama lay on the earth, and the world was shaken, Bharata, as when the sun falls."}},{"n":25,"text":"तत एनं सुसंविग्नाः सर्व एवाभिदुद्रुवुः ।\nतपोधनास्ते सहसा काश्या च भृगुनन्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the ascetics and the Kashi maiden ran to the descendant of Bhrigu, deeply distressed."}},{"n":26,"text":"त एनं संपरिष्वज्य शनैराश्वासयंस्तदा ।\nपाणिभिर्जलशीतैश्च जयाशीर्भिश्च कौरव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Embracing him, they slowly comforted him then with hands cool with water and blessings of victory, Kaurava."}},{"n":27,"text":"ततः स विह्वलो वाक्यं राम उत्थाय माब्रवीत् ।\nतिष्ठ भीष्म हतोऽसीति बाणं संधाय कार्मुके ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Rama, dazed, got up and said to me, fitting an arrow to his bow: Stand, Bhishma, you are killed."}},{"n":28,"text":"स मुक्तो न्यपतत्तूर्णं पार्श्वे सव्ये महाहवे ।\nयेनाहं भृशसंविग्नो व्याघूर्णित इव द्रुमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Released, that arrow fell quickly into my left side in the great fight, by which I was badly shaken, whirling like a tree."}},{"n":29,"text":"हत्वा हयांस्ततो राजञ्शीघ्रास्त्रेण महाहवे ।\nअवाकिरन्मां विश्रब्धो बाणैस्तैर्लोमवाहिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, after killing my horses in the great fight with his swift weapon, he confidently covered me with those arrows that flew with feathers."}},{"n":30,"text":"ततोऽहमपि शीघ्रास्त्रं समरेऽप्रतिवारणम् ।\nअवासृजं महाबाहो तेऽन्तराधिष्ठिताः शराः ।\nरामस्य मम चैवाशु व्योमावृत्य समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I too released the swift weapon, which cannot be warded off in battle, mighty-armed one; those arrows met in mid-air."}},{"n":31,"text":"न स्म सूर्यः प्रतपति शरजालसमावृतः ।\nमातरिश्वान्तरे तस्मिन्मेघरुद्ध इवानदत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of Rama and me, covering the sky all around, the sun did not shine, covered by the net of arrows; the wind, blocked in the space, roared as if shut in by clouds."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततो वायोः प्रकम्पाच्च सूर्यस्य च मरीचिभिः ।\nअभितापात्स्वभावाच्च पावकः समजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then from the wind's shaking, the sun's rays, the heat and their nature, fire arose."}},{"n":33,"text":"ते शराः स्वसमुत्थेन प्रदीप्ताश्चित्रभानुना ।\nभूमौ सर्वे तदा राजन्भस्मभूताः प्रपेदिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those arrows, blazing with fire of their own making, all fell to the ground then as ashes, king."}},{"n":34,"text":"तदा शतसहस्राणि प्रयुतान्यर्बुदानि च ।\nअयुतान्यथ खर्वाणि निखर्वाणि च कौरव ।\nरामः शराणां संक्रुद्धो मयि तूर्णमपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, Kaurava, Rama in anger quickly let fall on me hundreds of thousands, millions, tens of millions, and countless more arrows."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततोऽहं तानपि रणे शरैराशीविषोपमैः ।\nसंछिद्य भूमौ नृपतेऽपातयं पन्नगानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"I also cut those arrows in battle with arrows like venomous snakes and threw them down onto the ground, king, like snakes."}},{"n":36,"text":"एवं तदभवद्युद्धं तदा भरतसत्तम ।\nसंध्याकाले व्यतीते तु व्यपायात्स च मे गुरुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So that fight went on then, best of Bharatas, and when the twilight had passed, my teacher withdrew."}}]}]}